    "seconds": 51,
    "summary": "The anomaly is mitigated. The cause was a bad port mapping on the `user-service` Service, and I changed that one field.\n\n**What I found**\n- All 27 pods were Running and ready with zero restarts, so the problem was not a crash.\n- compose-post and nginx-thrift were failing every post request with `Connection refused` when connecting to `user-service:9090`.\n- The `user-service` Service mapped port 9090 to `targetPort: 9999`, but the container listens on 9090. As a result the Service endpoint was `10.244.1.160:9999`, where nothing was listening.\n- The other Services matched their containers. media-frontend maps 8081\u21928080, but it was already serving on 8080, so I left it alone.\n\n**What I changed**\n- Patched `svc/user-service` in `test-social-network` so `targetPort` is 9090 (from 9999). The endpoint is now `10.244.1.160:9090`.\n\n**Verification**\n- A direct TCP connection from compose-post to `user-service:9090` now succeeds.\n- Over a 30-second window after the patch, compose-post and nginx-thrift logged zero errors. The last error lines date from before the patch.\n\n**Not addressed**\n- social-graph-service logs warnings `GetFollowers: user_id ... not found` for several user IDs. This may be missing seed data rather than a fault in the service, and I did not investigate it because it is outside the reported failure.",
    "timed_out": false,
